  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "The equations \\(2x + 7 = 3\\) and \\(bx - 10 = -2\\) have the same solution \\(x.\\) What is the value of \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-8\\)",
    "B": "\\(-4\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Find the solution of the first equation so that we can use it in the second. Subtracting \\(7\\) from both sides and then dividing by \\(2\\) gives\n\\[\n2x=3-7=-4,\\qquad x=-2.\n\\]\nSince the second equation has this same solution, substitute \\(x=-2\\):\n\\[\n-2b-10=-2.\n\\]\nAdding \\(10\\) to both sides gives \\(-2b=8\\). Dividing by the nonzero number \\(-2\\), we obtain \\(b=-4\\). Indeed, \\((-4)(-2)-10=-2\\), as required. Therefore the answer is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\), choice B.",
